2. For each entity or attribute, check whether the conversation history contains at least one <tool_call> with a search query that mentions that entity or attribute (case-insensitive substring match against any search query argument).
3. If all entities and attributes are covered by at least one search query, output: { "missing": [] }
4. If any entity or attribute has no matching search query, output: { "missing": ["<exact missing entity or attribute>"] } — list only the first missing item.

Return only valid JSON. No other text.
